      "writtenOn": "2024-01-14T08:57:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doclava ends the first sentence of the javadoc at the first period (see go/android-api-guidelines#period). So only \"Returns the service type.\" will show up in the public method table. One concrete example is the NsdServiceInfo#getAttributes API listed in the given link.\n\nBut \"Returns the service type.\" provides no additional meaningful information than what a developer can get from the API method name (`getServiceType()`). It makes the summary useless when it\u0027s shown in the method table.\n\nSo I made changes:\n1. To say that the service name is dot-joint string of two labels.\n2 Move the examples to the description section.\n\nPlease unresolve this if it doesn\u0027t look good to you.",
      "parentUuid": "6147720d_0e071338",
      "revId": "8c579990cfb6ef89650caf4221d8960351325d43",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
